      "writtenOn": "2021-03-23T10:27:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Todd,\n\nreset_timer_v1 which we have added with this patch just extends the logic from reset_timer() which is android specific code in android kernel branch and not available in upstream.\n\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android-mainline/net/netfilter/xt_IDLETIMER.c#371\n\nUpstream: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git/tree/net/netfilter/xt_IDLETIMER.c\n\nTherefore, this patch is android specific. When the original change to add ALARM timer in upstream was created by us, we didn\u0027t add any reset_timer_v1 as kernel didn\u0027t have reset_timer originally. Refer to the following commit which was picked from upstream onto Google kernel branch:\ncommit\t68983a354a655c35d3fb204489d383a2a051fda7\nnetfilter: xtables: Add snapshot of hardidletimer target\n\nThere are few additional changes which I agree are not related to reset_timer logic and we\u0027ll remove those.",
